    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I changed to satisfy the spec:\n\n## Summary\n\n**`Owner.getMembershipLevel()`** (`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`) \u2014 Previously it capped at 3 and level 4 was only documented as \"reserved for tenure\" but was never reachable. Now:\n- Creation-time factors (start at 1, +1 for email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are still capped at 3.\n- After the cap, it adds a further +1 **only when tenure exceeds 365 days**, measured as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today (zero tenure), the tenure bump never applies, so a new owner never exceeds level 3 \u2014 matching the example in the spec (email + `namesakeCount` 0 + 3-member household \u2192 level 3, not 4). Level 4 is now genuinely reachable only for owners with more than 365 days of tenure.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Updated the `membershipLevel` schema: `maximum` raised from 3 to 4 and the description rewritten to state that level 4 requires tenure of more than 365 days.\n\nThe existing acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (which asserts a brand-new owner with an email and no namesake lands at level 3) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).",
